import Riemann.Deep.FirstZero.MinCert5

/-!
# Minimality of the first certified zero of ζ

Fayed.FirstZero.no_zero_below: ζ has no zero with 0 < Re s < 1 and 0 < Im s < 14.13.
Fayed.FirstZero.first_zero_is_first: the certified zero 1/2 + it₁ (14.13 < t₁ < 14.14) has the
smallest positive ordinate among all zeros in the critical strip.
Fayed.FirstZero.zeros_below_15: it is the only zero in the strip with 0 < Im s ≤ 15.

Route: argument principle for ζ on [1/4, 2] × [−15, 15] (simple pole at 1, conjugation symmetry),
arg change along 2 → 2 + 15i → 1/4 + 15i → 1/4 certified < 3π by Euler–Maclaurin Taylor models on
30 segments (MinCert*.lean, generated by .scratch/minimality/drive.py).
-/

